# {{ c.mcp_dist }}

An [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server for the {{ c.title }}. It wraps the
[`{{ c.dist }}`](https://pypi.org/project/{{ c.dist }}/) Python SDK and exposes one tool per
API method, named `<resource>_<method>`:

{% for t in c.tools %}
- `{{ t.name }}`: {{ t.title }}
{% endfor %}

## Install

```sh
pip install {{ c.mcp_dist }}
```

Requires Python 3.10 or newer.

## Run

The server speaks MCP over stdio.

```sh
{% if c.env_key %}
export {{ c.env_key }}=...
{% endif %}
{{ c.mcp_dist }}
```

Example client configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{ c.pkg }}": {
      "command": "{{ c.mcp_dist }}"{% if c.env_key %},
      "env": { "{{ c.env_key }}": "..." }{% endif %}

    }
  }
}
```

Tool results are JSON. Binary responses are written to the directory in
`{{ c.env_output_dir }}` (a temporary directory by default) and the tool returns the file's path
and size. Set `{{ c.env_base_url }}` to point the server at a different API host.
